infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same callback slot, two declaration forms
  desc on(handler: (e: Event) => void) — only the syntax differs, yet the variance flips
  compares
    - label Method shorthand  on(handler)
      children
        - label Parameter is bivariant
          desc By design, even under strictFunctionTypes
        - label Narrow (e: MouseEvent) handler
          desc Accepted with no error — unsound
        - label Blows up at runtime
          desc A plain Event arrives, e.button is undefined
        - label strictFunctionTypes
          desc Does not tighten method params
    - label Property function  on: (handler) => void
      children
        - label Parameter is contravariant
          desc The sound direction is enforced
        - label Narrow (e: MouseEvent) handler
          desc Rejected at compile time
        - label Caught before it ships
          desc Type error points straight at the hole
        - label strictFunctionTypes
          desc Tightens standalone fn params (TS 2.6)
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
